+++ b/docs/uninstall.md
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Uninstall Hive
+
+Run `hive uninstall` (or `hv uninstall`) to validate the installation receipt,
+stop and unregister the user service, and delegate core removal to Homebrew,
+`paru`/`yay`, or the shell channel.
+
+By default, all user work is preserved:
+
+- XDG config, data, cache, and state
+- `.hive-state` tasks, logs, completed outputs, and worktrees
+- every project `.hive/` file
+- all agent skills and marketplace packages
+
+To remove generated project scaffold files, pass an absolute project path with
+`--project-cleanup`. `--purge` makes that same narrow cleanup
+non-interactive. Both modes remove only regular, unmodified files whose digest
+matches `.hive/ownership.yml`. Modified files, unknown files, symlinks,
+path-escaping entries, state, completed work, and agent skills remain
+preserved. Hive never recursively deletes `.hive/` or `.hive-state/`.
